# The React UI source and build.
#
# Excluded because the container never serves it: like the vanilla static/index.html in a deployed
# setup, the built React app is published to S3 and served by CloudFront (deploy_ui.py). app.py's
# /react route exists for local development, and reports that the build is absent rather than
# failing when it is, which is exactly the right answer inside the container.
#
# node_modules/ and dist/ are already covered above; this makes the intent explicit and keeps ~2 MB
# of TypeScript source out of every image build.
ui/

# Tests. Both bare and **/-prefixed: Docker matches .dockerignore patterns root-relative, so a bare
# pattern misses nested copies. requirements-dev.txt is excluded for the same reason the image carries no
# test runner.
test_*.py
**/test_*.py
requirements-dev.txt
